type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dabbs"
    given-names: "Garrick"
    email: "garrickdabbs@gmail.com"
abstract: >-
  SFM Core is an experimental Python framework implementing F. Gregory Hayden's
  Social Fabric Matrix (SFM) methodology for analyzing institutional systems
  through graph-based networks. The framework provides 40+ specialized node types
  across 12 analytical domains, dual-backend architecture (NetworkX/Neo4j),
  REST API, and advanced analysis methods including ceremonial vs instrumental
  classification, circular causation detection, and temporal modeling. This is
  research software with known structural differences from Hayden's canonical
  approach (documented in SFM_FIDELITY_ANALYSIS.md). Extensive AI assistance
  (Claude AI) was used in development.
keywords:
  - social-fabric-matrix
  - institutional-economics
  - heterodox-economics
  - graph-analysis
  - policy-analysis
  - ceremonial-instrumental
  - circular-causation
  - hayden
  - network-analysis
